{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EWjNSAT6VhKECzGWrgmR2x","type":"tool_result","content":"=== STAGE.md\nBuild the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\n=== TASK.md hand-in lines\n7:Game Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\n11:Package: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is ea\n19:Audio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\n23:Working Environment and deliverable:\n24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105\n89:## Done\n90:No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you ca\n=== test.mjs: what full means\n8:const ALL = ['unit', 'flow', 'events', 'balance', 'input', 'audio', 'hub', 'ui'];\n10:if (!groups.length || groups.includes('full')) groups = ALL;\nok   html named as TASK says, in this folder 3.87 MB\nok   dev subfolder named as TASK says \nok   dev files: bundled from separate modules 91 source modules\nok   PROGRESS.md kept (STAGE.md) \nok   exit-interview.json beside the html \nok   interview parses, top-level keys exact \nok   sourceInformation keys exact, all filled \nok   date, environment, model match TASK.md \nok   usage reads added on import \nok   4, 6 and 4 feedback answers \nok   aiHub keys exact \nok   aiHub genre from the list, 3-6 lowercase tags \nok   html title matches aiHub name \nok   session client directly after meta charset \nok   no external script or stylesheet \nok   About data generated from this interview \nok   no TODO, FIXME or placeholder in src \nok   no audio files in the project \nok   music defaults to 10 \nok   issues tally has 37 lines, as the interview says \nchecksum 4215b27c33898065 | 20 of 20 ok","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e","uuid":"558e7822-8801-423d-92e7-0f63bc08b3f7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T13:51:36.233Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== STAGE.md\nBuild the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\n=== TASK.md hand-in lines\n7:Game Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\n11:Package: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is ea\n19:Audio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\n23:Working Environment and deliverable:\n24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105\n89:## Done\n90:No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo