{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0157eXxkc6SdUatjECDkA6AV","type":"tool_result","content":"=== PLAN.md section 19 checklist\n**Done means** no TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features: the demo is complete. Before you finish, check every line:\n\n- [ ] Single HTML where TASK.md says, opens from `file://`, no external requests, no audio files\n- [ ] WebGPU backend by default, WebGL2 fallback works, cel-shaded with the ink filter, Rapier 0.19.3, Three R180, Web Audio, Gamepad API\n- [ ] Original cast, events, art and music; title is your own random pick; nothing from section 2's lists\n- [ ] All thirteen events, or the ones left after cuts, each with tiers, an intro, results and bots\n- [ ] Programme through the ending, Wobble Age graph, jar, unlocks, Free Play\n- [ ] Controller-first; keyboard and mouse native on the same screens; prompts follow last device; Xbox glyph option; no dense screens\n- [ ] Attract at 10 s, any input exits; Dev Mode from Pause with tools, live sliders and reset; touch-only message and Settings\n- [ ] Group Class 1-4 on one screen; hub harness passes at 1, 2, 4 players, on the bad network, with the host leaving; game on its own passes Enter and Space\n- [ ] Music at 10% by default; all sound in code; gibberish voices with every word on screen\n- [ ] `node tools/test.mjs full` passes; a scripted whole-game playthrough is part of it\n- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubs in `src/`\n- [ ] About/Credits, the exit-interview file and your chat reply are all filled in as below\n\n=== Registry and tiers\nexport const EVENT_CLASSES = { fruitHat: FruitHat, poses: Poses, cairn: Cairn, stillWater: StillWater, logReps: LogReps, plank: Plank, tug: Tug, stepClass: StepClass, plates: Plates, islandLoop: IslandLoop, roomService: RoomService, springboard: Springboard, r\n14 events; poses:3 cairn:3 stillWater:3 logReps:3 plank:3 tug:3 stepClass:3 plates:3 islandLoop:3 fruitHat:3 roomService:3 springboard:3 raft:3 grandHold:3\nevery event has intro words and verbs: true\ncairn.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\nfruitHat.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\ngrandHold.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\nislandLoop.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\nlogReps.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\nplank.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\nplates.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\nposes.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\nraft.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\nroomService.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\nspringboard.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\nstepClass.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\nstillWater.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\ntug.js botInput:1 laneResult:1\n\n=== Title and modes in the build\n2:export const TITLE = 'We Fib';\nattract.js checkin.js devmode.js director.js ending.js eventRun.js flow.js ghost.js groupclass.js hub.js jar.js programme.js results.js session.js \n\n=== exit-interview.json (final)\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-05 04:44:42\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Physics-balance party sports with a daily-ritual progression\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Third person: framed stage cameras per event, and an orbitable chase camera on the island\",\n    \"tech\": \"Three.js R180 (three 0.180.0) on the WebGPU backend with WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon materials and ink post, Rapier 0.19.3 (rapier3d-compat), Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Fredoka 5.3.0 (fontsource), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"Cel-shaded ink filter over a sun-bleached wooden-toy resort; every model made in code from Three.js primitives and toon materials\",\n    \"animation\": \"Three.js AnimationMixer clips on jointed rigs, procedural lean, bobble and breath from the physics, Rapier ragdolls built from the rig\",\n    \"audio\": \"Code-synthesised city-pop and bossa at 10% by default, synthesised sound effects, Animalese and Simlish-style gibberish voices with every word on screen; no audio files\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 players on one screen with Group Class\",\n    \"testing\": \"Allowed: as much headless testing as wanted, scripts that play the game and check its state including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, one command printing only failures and a one-line count, screenshots only for what a script can't check, no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Ran: node tools/test.mjs with eight groups and about 1,670 checks: whole-game playthrough by bots on a stubbed pad, every event and tier, balance tables over three seeds, every verb on pad, keys and mouse, offline audio renders, the hub harness at 1, 2 and 4 players, bad network and host leaving, the 1080p layout audit, touch profiles, a WebGL2 boot in WebKit, plus a screenshot art pass. Not run: real controller, real TV, human ears, a human player.\",\n    \"research\": \"The AI Hub protocol README and harness files from the hub repository. No further research on the source beyond what PLAN.md already held.\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\",\n    \"usage\": \"added on import\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"37 logged in notes/issues.md as they happened: 33 caught by test scripts and screenshots, 4 found by reading code paths after the scripts passed.\",\n    \"11: Hop presses lost during hit-stop, every Tug of Peace doll falling, the Springboard crash, two Rapier panics on later dives, divers teleporting in mid-air, the game stuck at the first Wobble Age, the finale's doll hidden inside the lamp, Step Class footprints hidden behind the doll, Trudy's lean tutorial being impossible, and Enter on the session card missing the hub's time limit under load, which would have kept the game out of sessions.\",\n    \"The scripted whole-game playthrough with bots on a stubbed pad. It got stuck on real flow bugs no single event test could show, including the first Wobble Age and the lean tutorial, and it runs the whole game in about a minute of machine time.\",\n    \"The per-event rendered smoke run and the WebKit boot. Both passed the first time and changed nothing, though they remain worth keeping as guards.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"toonOutlinePass plus a short TSL pass gave the whole ink look, the same on WebGPU and WebGL2. Rapier is also very fast: a minute of play at 120 Hz simulates in about a second.\",\n    \"Yes. Rapier panics caught me most: disabling a core after removing its joint panicked world.step on a later dive, and every call after that reported a misleading recursive-use error. I first took that for a bug in my own test.\",\n    \"The balance core and the lane system, then a fixed-step game that runs entirely on sim time, so a test can play the whole game headlessly by calling advance().\",\n    \"Knowing where a failure really started. A Rapier panic surfaces in a later call with a message about something else, and with software rendering each visual check takes a long time, so most judgement had to come from state instead of from looking.\",\n    \"None.\",\n    \"Make a Rapier panic a catchable error that names the call and the handle, instead of poisoning every later call on the page.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"Open creative choices combined with exact, checkable facts about the machine and the hub, and a plan whose numbers were measured rather than guessed.\",\n    \"How to write a source with a space in the file name, and what the engine's native style and asset library mean for Three.js, which has neither. The plan answered the second.\",\n    \"Judging feel with no player. Scripts can prove an event is winnable, losable and separates skill levels, but not that it is fun. Bots also agreed too easily until I gave them human faults.\",\n    \"Say how to tell memory pressure from other runs apart from a real crash in practice, since a shared machine with full swap can kill a long test. Ask for one short recorded video of play, so that feel has at least one more check.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"We Fib\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Level with us. Eventually.\",\n    \"description\": \"A wooden-toy wellness retreat on a crooked island, where you hold poses, stack stones and catch fruit with real balance physics, and straighten the whole island one class at a time.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Feet: L2 R2, Q E or clicks. Flail: Square or F\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"comedy\", \"third-person\", \"versus\", \"arcade\"]\n  }\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e","uuid":"f683ffb9-6a1e-4f84-9c15-5ec43d39c022","timestamp":"2026-11-05T13:52:05.530Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== PLAN.md section 19 checklist\n**Done means** no TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features: the demo is complete. Before you finish, check every line:\n\n- [ ] Single HTML where TASK.md says, opens from `file://`, no external requests, no audio files\n- [ ] WebGPU backend by default, WebGL2 fallback works, cel-shaded with the ink filter, Rapier 0.19.3, Three R180, Web Audio, Gamepad API\n- [ ] Original cast, events, art and music; title is your own random pick; nothing from section 2's lists\n- [ ] All thirteen events, or the ones left after cuts, each with tiers, an intro, results and bots\n- [ ] Programme through the ending, Wobble Age graph, jar, unlocks, Free Play\n- [ ] Controller-first; keyboard and mouse native on the same screens; prompts follow last device; Xbox glyph option; no dense screens\n- [ ] Attract at 10 s, any input exits; Dev Mode from Pause with tools, live sliders and reset; touch-only message and Settings\n- [ ] Group Class 1-4 on one screen; hub harness passes at 1, 2, 4 players, on the bad network, with the host leaving; game on its own passes