{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjttdPd4RvbP7B8emhfJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All eight test groups pass on the final build, and nothing was cut from the plan. The checksum was `4215b27c33898065` before and after, and the group counts add up to the same 1666 as the full run.\n\n| Group | Passed | Failed |\n|---|---|---|\n| `unit` | 1027 | 0 |\n| `flow` | 48 | 0 |\n| `events` | 263 | 0 |\n| `balance` | 42 | 0 |\n| `input` | 35 | 0 |\n| `audio` | 175 | 0 |\n| `hub` | 9 | 0 |\n| `ui` | 67 | 0 |\n\n**PLAN.md section 19 checklist**\n\n| Item | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Single HTML, opens from `file://`, no external requests or audio files | File in place at 3.87 MB; a smoke run from `file://` made 0 external requests; `unit` checks for audio files and external scripts |\n| WebGPU, WebGL2 fallback, ink, Rapier 0.19.3, Three R180, Web Audio, Gamepad API | `events` confirms WebGPU with the device alive on all 14 events, and the WebGL2 fallback in WebKit; `flow` confirms both versions; ink checked by eye in the art pass; the Gamepad API was tested through a stand-in pad |\n| Original work, title a random pick, nothing from section 2's lists | Search of `src` for the banned activities and product words found none; title picked with `secrets.choice` from 50; originality of the art is my judgement from screenshots |\n| All events, each with tiers, an intro, results and bots | 14 registered (13 plus the finale), nothing cut; each has 3 tiers, intro text, a result and a bot; `events` runs every tier to the end |\n| Programme through the ending, graph, jar, unlocks, Free Play | `flow` plays Day 1 through the ending into a Maintenance day; the tilt reaches exactly 0 and Free Play has all 14; `ui` walks the Journal, including the graph |\n| Controller-first, native keys and mouse, prompts follow device, Xbox glyphs, no dense screens | `input` covers each device and the glyph switch; `ui` audits every screen at 1080p for text size, safe area and at most six choices |\n| Attract at 10 s, Dev Mode from Pause, touch-only message | `flow` covers attract timing, each device exiting it, and every Dev page and slider reset; `ui` covers three touch profiles |\n| Group Class 1-4, hub harness, game on its own | `input` joins four pads and checks each controls its own lane; `hub` passes at 1, 2 and 4 players, bad network and host leaving, plus Enter and Space on its own |\n| Music at 10%, all sound in code, gibberish voices on screen | `audio` confirms the default of 10 and bus gain 0.10, and renders every track, sting, effect and voice offline |\n| `full` passes, including a whole-game playthrough | 1666 passed, 0 failed; the playthrough is in `flow` |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | `unit` searches every source file |\n| About, exit interview and chat reply filled in | `ui` compares About with the interview file; the file's final contents are printed above and match the feedback in my earlier report |\n\nI also checked the plan's tone guard: the only body or food words in the dialogue are the plan's own, \"belly flop\" and Coach's lunch line.\n\n**Still unverified:** nobody has played it with a real controller, on a real TV or with human ears, and no person has judged whether it's fun. Those can't be done on this computer. Balance figures come from bots modelling people, and mouse play was tested for input but not for skill."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":445,"cache_read_input_tokens":791801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":445},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e","uuid":"d9dfeffa-f233-43ba-ab54-8e008bc4a387","timestamp"