{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgjumch86vz9tbxfv4Ww6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`node tools/test.mjs full` on the final build gives **1743 passed, 0 failed**, and the file's checksum (`cd7de6b05a2ce54d`) was the same before and after the run.\n\n| Group | Passed | Failed |\n|---|---|---|\n| `unit` | 1027 | 0 |\n| `flow` (includes the whole-game playthrough) | 48 | 0 |\n| `events` | 263 | 0 |\n| `balance` | 119 | 0 |\n| `input` | 35 | 0 |\n| `audio` | 175 | 0 |\n| `hub` | 9 | 0 |\n| `ui` | 67 | 0 |\n\n**What changed since my last report**\n- **Log Reps on keys and mouse:** I ran the bots through real key and pointer events, and they exposed a real flaw. One late press left you behind for the whole rep, scoring 82/33/18 against the stick's 96/81/58. After the fix it scores 97/88/66, so it's fair, though now a little easier than the stick. Still Water is the other gap: its clumsy bot scores only 12–16 on keys and mouse against 82 on the stick. Its check only requires at least 10, because that bot oscillates in the small zone; I left the plan's tuned numbers alone.\n- **Final art pass:** I redid it on the final visuals, including the Day 1 and Day 5 islands, and found nothing to change. That's my judgement from screenshots.\n- **Plan checklist:** every section 19 item still holds, as listed in my last message; only the test counts above changed.\n\n**Can't be done on this computer:** nobody has tried it with a real controller, on a real TV or with human ears, and no person has played it. TASK.md says these are \"never required\", and I tested with its stand-ins. So whether it's fun is still unproven, and the skill figures come from bots modelling people.\n\n**Corrected answers:** the rest of my earlier report stands, including the Engine and Prompt Feedback. These two fields replace what I sent before, and `exit-interview.json` and the About screen match them:\n- **Testing (Source Information):** Allowed: as much headless testing as wanted, scripts that play the game and check its state including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, one command printing only failures and a one-line count, screenshots only for what a script can't check, no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Ran: node tools/test.mjs with eight groups and about 1,740 checks: whole-game playthrough by bots on a stubbed pad, every event and tier, balance tables over three seeds, the same bots again through real key and pointer events, every verb on pad, keys and mouse, offline audio renders, the hub harness at 1, 2 and 4 players, bad network and host leaving, the 1080p layout audit, touch profiles, a WebGL2 boot in WebKit, plus a screenshot art pass. Not run: real controller, real TV, human ears, a human player.\n- **Testing Feedback 1:** 39 logged in notes/issues.md as they happened: 35 caught by test scripts and screenshots, 4 found by reading code paths after the scripts passed.\n- **Testing Feedback 3:** The scripted whole-game playthrough with bots on a stubbed pad. It got stuck on real flow bugs no single event test could show, including the first Wobble Age and the lean tutorial, and it runs the whole game in about a minute of machine time. Running the same bots through real keys and mouse came second: it found Log Reps unfair on keys, late in the build.\n\nEverything is in `work/`, and nothing is committed to git:\n- `WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442/` (dev files)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1087,"cache_read_input_tokens":829840,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1087},"output_tokens":743,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"d