{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjzhUZTAsiCawqwXxhCu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The goal is met: nothing in `PLAN.md` that can be done on this computer is left open, and every hand-in is in the folder. `STAGE.md` and `TASK.md` are printed in full above, along with the plan's section 21 coverage table. That table was the last thing I hadn't walked row by row.\n\n**What the section 21 walk found**\nIt turned up three proofs I hadn't written, all test-only:\n- attract actually looping through all nine vignettes and back to the title\n- a click exiting attract\n- clips changing\n\nAll three now pass, so every row with a test named in that table is met. The checksum stayed `bf5310f7efa48633`, because the game file didn't change.\n\n**Test counts on that file:** the last full run was 2022 passed, 0 failed. Since then I've added 13 more checks and re-run the two groups they're in: `flow` 57 passed, `events` 286 passed. That makes 2035 checks in total, with no failures. The interview's \"about 2,020 checks\" still describes the full run, and I left it rather than rebuild for such a small difference.\n\n**The remaining objections are things the source documents treat as open:**\n\n| Objection | What the documents say |\n|---|---|\n| Real controller, TV, human ears | `TASK.md`: \"No script can check these… Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\" I used its stand-ins: stubbed pads, `OfflineAudioContext`, 1080p screenshots |\n| A human player, and whether it's fun | `PLAN.md` section 20: \"Whether it is fun is yours to judge.\" I can only offer the bots and screenshots |\n| Originality, tone, art | Section 21 lists the proof as \"your art pass and judgement\", backed by the `unit` searches. I did that pass on the final visuals |\n| Still Water on keys and mouse | The plan's own measurement for a clumsy player is 28 on keys and 24 on stick, in `PLAN.md` line 82. My 12–16 is a different metric (the form score) but tells the same story: that bot struggles here. My stick score of 78 is what stands out, because the pad's dead zone hides its jitter. I left the plan's tuning alone, and my check for it only requires at least 10 |\n\nThose last three are judgement calls, and you're welcome to disagree with them after trying the game. The first two rows are the real limits of this computer, so a person with a controller is the one check still worth doing.\n\nThe Source Information and all the feedback answers in my previous message are the final versions, and `exit-interview.json` and the About screen match them. Nothing is committed to git."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10516,"cache_read_input_tokens":934045,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10516},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e","uuid":"813128d8-0352-4ed3-a7c5-921626eca017","timestamp":"2026-11-05T15:11:45.699Z","request_id":"req_011CgjzhU3SqW5LNVCxFMHfr"}
