{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, ScheduleWakeup, ToolSearch</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - The user set a goal: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n   - STAGE.md says in full: \"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\"\n   - TASK.md asks for an original game inspired by Wii Fit, delivered as:\n     - a single HTML file `[GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442].html` in root\n     - a dev subfolder of the same name\n     - `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML\n     - Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in the chat reply and on an in-game About/Credits screen\n   - Required stack: Three.js R180, WebGPU, cel-shaded/ink filter, Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, Gamepad API.\n   - Also required: all audio in code, music at 10% by default, gibberish voices, dev mode from Pause with live sliders and reset, attract mode after 10 s, AI Hub multiplayer plus the game on its own, 10-foot controller-first UI, touch-only message with Settings, no TODOs or stubs.\n   - Standing constraints, which must stay in effect:\n     - \"Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one.\"\n     - \"Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools.\"\n     - Any server binds 127.0.0.1 on an OS-picked port, and I confirm the page is my game.\n     - \"Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"\n     - \"Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check. Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"\n     - \"Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\"\n     - \"Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder.\"\n     - \"don't run playwright install or playwright install-deps.\"\n     - Use `uv run --with ...` for Python packages.\n     - Git: commit or push only when the user asks (nothing has been committed).\n     - The user's email is only for identifying the user and must never be sent to unrelated services.\n     - Use they/them for anyone whose pronouns aren't stated.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Three.js r180 `three/webgpu` and `three/tsl`, with WebGPU backend and WebGL2 fallback.\n   - `toonOutlinePass` plus a TSL ink post pass with boil, grain, vignette and ink-blot wipe uniform; `MeshToonNodeMaterial` with a 3-step ramp.\n   - Rapier 0.19.3 compat. Balance core: a dynamic body on a spherical joint to a kinematic foot, driven by a torque-limited spring with gravity feed-forward. Collision groups by lane; ragdolls built from the rig.\n   - Island tilt by tilting gravity, not by moving the disc.\n   - Fixed 1/120 s sim, with generator scripts on sim time (`Scripts`, `Handle`), no setTimeout in src, and `Loop.advance()` for tests.\n   - Lane system (local, bot, ghost), with bots modelled as delayed correction (sharp, average, clumsy).\n   - Input with latched presses, the `buttons` bitmask, an asking ring for keys, and `lastDevice` for prompts. Inline SVG glyphs carry `data-glyph`.\n   - AnimationMixer clips on jointed rigs through `poseClip`.\n   - All-code Web Audio: FM instruments, a look-ahead sequencer, data-driven tracks, formant gibberish voices, OfflineAudioContext probes.\n   - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode with its own card, client 1.4.0 (hash-checked), timeline on `AIHub.time()`.\n   - esbuild single-file build; Fredoka fonts inlined; Playwright 1.63.0 tests. RENDER flags: `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - Root `work/`:\n     - `PLAN.md`, `STAGE.md`, `TASK.md` (inputs)\n     - `PROGRESS.md` (kept up to date; says 49 issues; its text no longer quotes a checksum)\n     - `WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442.html` (final, 3.87 MB, sha256 starts `0c248c52e7eecd04`)\n     - `exit-interview.json` (final; Testing field says \"about 2,035 checks\"; Testing Feedback 1 says 49 logged, 38 caught by test scripts, measurements and screenshots, 11 found by reading code paths and checking the build line by line against the plan; Testing Feedback 2 says 11 critical; usage \"added on import\"; aiHub name \"We Fib\", tagline \"Level with us. Eventually.\", genre Sports, players \"1–4\", series empty)\n   - Dev folder `WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442/`, about 91 source modules:\n     - `src/main.js`\n     - `src/core/` (loop, rng, save, script, tuning, testHooks)\n     - `src/data/` (config [TITLE = 'We Fib'], events, programme, poses, charts, dialogue, tuning, palettes, unlocks, names, aboutPages, about [generated by the build from the interview])\n     - `src/physics/` (world, balancer, ragdoll, island)\n     - `src/render/` (ink, palette, sky, sea, cameraRig, particles, comicText)\n     - `src/art/` (materials, doll, cast, props, island)\n     - `src/anim/` (rig, clips)\n     - `src/input/` (input, glyphs, bot)\n     - `src/audio/` (engine, instruments, tracks, sequencer, sfx, voice, probe)\n     - `src/ui/` (ui.css, ui.js, dom, speech, disc, hud, diagrams, screens/{settings, about, journal, pause, confirm, plan, mirror, sessionOptions})\n     - `src/game/` (director, programme, eventRun, flow, hub, jar, checkin, ending, attract, devmode, groupclass, session, ghost, results)\n     - `src/events/` (base, index, poses, cairn, stillWater, logReps, plank, tug, stepClass, plates, islandLoop, fruitHat, roomService, springboard, raft, grandHold)\n     - `tools/` (build.mjs, about.mjs, lib.mjs, test.mjs, test-flow.mjs, test-input.mjs, test-audio.mjs, test-hub.mjs, test-ui.mjs, shots.mjs, hub/{harness.html, bridge.js, round.js})\n     - `vendor/session.js`\n     - `notes/issues.md` (49 numbered issues), `notes/hub-README.md`\n   - Commands:\n     - `node tools/build.mjs`\n     - `node tools/test.mjs [unit flow events balance input audio hub ui full]` (optional `PER_GROUP=1`, `INFO=1`)\n     - `node tools/shots.mjs [names]`\n   - `tools/lib.mjs` provides `silence(page)`, `availableGB()`, `waitForRoom()` and `isMemoryCrash()`. `tools/test.mjs` waits for free memory before each group and retries a crashed group once from a clean count.\n\n4. Errors and fixes (49 in `notes/issues.md`; the key ones):\n   - Hit-stop swallowed input presses. Fixed by holding input polling during hit-stop.\n   - Fruit landed short of its shadow ring because of linear damping. Fixed.\n   - Tug's kinematic foot teleport threw the core over. Fixed: the foot stays put, and only the visible doll moves.\n   - Springboard crashed because the base class recovered the ragdoll first. Fixed with a separate water state.\n   - Rapier panics on later dives from a re-created joint on a disabled body and from `setEnabled(false)` on a free core. Fixed with `park()`/`unpark()`.\n   - God-mode stand-up teleported divers mid-air. Fixed: no fall checks in the air.\n   - Raft slope push was too weak, and Room Service's side jolt spilled glasses. Both fixed.\n   - A bot's `useMove` flag leaked between events. Fixed in `blankInput`.\n   - Could not pause during barks; Use couldn't advance speech on reveal and jar; the swallow blocked unconnected pads; Use also activated the focused island thing; the lean tutorial was blocked by `uiBusy`. All fixed.\n   - Music clipped at slider 100. Fixed with a trim (`musicIn` 0.36).\n   - Safe-area layout problems, the doll hidden in the finale lamp, the ring road through landmarks, the raft sinking, the dark Step Class floor, plates covering the doll, Step Class prints hidden behind the doll, the attract overlay removed by vignettes, and the Grand Hold playable before other classes. All fixed.\n   - Bugs found by reading code: mouse pumping launched instantly in Springboard (fixed with a `launch` verb); Esc closed and reopened Pause, Options couldn't close it, and Esc on a menu also paused; session events called begin() twice; attract's Step Class skip was reset. All fixed.\n   - Enter on the session card was read in the sim tick, so it missed the hub's 3 s limit under load. Fixed: `onCardKey` answers from the keydown event.\n   - Log Reps on keys could never recover from a late press. Fixed with a catch-up at rate 1.6.\n   - Plan audit items, all built or written:\n     - Simlish exclamations never spoken\n     - flail penalties missing in Cairn and Still Water\n     - bedsheet with no collider\n     - no wave before swells, and no band colour on the hoop\n     - marbles didn't flare; sleep and peck clips unused\n     - softened balance thresholds restored (sharp 85, clumsy 40, Room Service all five)\n     - missing tests written (soak, pixel read-back, Lean Match, tier rules, boot failure, pad disconnect, island mouse controls, attract loop, click exit, clips change)\n     - bots ignored the seed, so \"three seeds\" was often one. Fixed.\n   - Bedsheet catch and marble flare happened off camera. Fixed: the camera follows the fall to a sheet held by the class, placed clear of the tower with SHEET_X/SHEET_Z, and the camera cuts wide for the flare.\n   - Marbles were white in normal play because `instanceColor` didn't exist before the first draw. Fixed with initial `setColorAt` and dynamic usage, plus pixel tests.\n   - Browser \"Target crashed\" in long runs: sound nodes piled up because the sim runs about 170x real time, on a machine with full swap. I wrongly said \"no leak\" and then \"real leak\"; the final measurement shows it isn't a leak in play (981 MB drains to 192 MB in about a minute; flat at 290 MB with audio off). Fixed in tests: silent except the audio group, with static name checks for sounds, tracks, stings and clips.\n   - My own tool slips:\n     - a stray `cat > /tmp/.x` hung a command for 10 minutes (empty file removed)\n     - a `cd WeFib*` glob failed and invalidated one audit (re-run correctly)\n     - the shell's cwd persisted in `notes/shots` once (re-run from the dev folder)\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Final verification on the final file (checksum `0c248c52e7eecd04`, before and after): `node tools/test.mjs full` gives **2035 passed, 0 failed**, made up of unit 1272, flow 57, events 286, balance 124, input 44, audio 175, hub 9, ui 68. No crash notes.\n   - About vs interview, sentence by sentence: 11 pages, 29 values, 58 sentences, 0 missing. Credits include Fredoka, Three.js, Rapier and We Fib.\n   - PLAN.md section 19 checklist printed (lines 835-848) and each line mapped to named tests in the transcript. Two names with template syntax (`tier ${tier + 1} completes`, `hub ${name} passes`) didn't match the grep but exist in the tools.\n   - STAGE.md and TASK.md printed in full, and PLAN section 21 printed and walked.\n   - Art pass on the final visuals done by eye via `tools/shots.mjs`.\n   - Things that can't be settled here:\n     - Real controller, TV, human ears, human player. TASK.md: \"Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\"\n     - Fun, originality, art and tone are my judgement. PLAN section 21 lists \"your art pass and judgement\" as the proof; PLAN section 20 says \"Whether it is fun is yours to judge.\"\n   - Known weak result: Still Water on keys and mouse, clumsy bot 12–16. That is in line with the plan's own measurement at PLAN line 82: \"Still Water Tier 1 100 / 85 / 28 (100 / 93 / 24)\". The check's floor is 10, and tuning was left alone.\n   - Keys and mouse Log Reps score 97/88/66, a little easier than the stick's 96/81/58.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"/goal Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n   - Stop-hook feedback messages (repeated, each quoting the goal), objecting to:\n     - the full suite not being re-run across all groups after the last changes\n     - STAGE.md and TASK.md not visibly read\n     - hand-in checks not shown against the actual text\n     - the `ui` group and per-group output and checksum not shown on the final build\n     - PLAN's full checklist not walked item by item\n     - judgement items (originality, ink look, art quality, tone) resting on my own judgement\n     - playtesting not done and mouse skill not checked\n     - the withdrawn \"every checklist item holds\" claim\n     - Still Water on keys and mouse as a known weak spot\n     - interview counts not cleanly re-verified against the About screen after the last edit\n   - A goal check-in message about background task bltlhqisc: \"Check on their progress... If they are progressing, say so briefly and keep waiting; if they are stuck or no longer needed, fix or stop them and continue toward the goal.\"\n   - The latest stop-hook message repeats that the condition isn't established because of no line-by-line checklist check in the transcript, judgement items, the Still Water weak result, and the withdrawn claim. It then instructs: respond with text only, no tool calls, and produce this summary.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - No build, test or code work is outstanding. All hand-ins are in `work/`.\n   - No commit was requested,