{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011kkJHir3vrY674JD4Fh56W","type":"tool_result","content":"--- slider tests in tools\ntools/test-flow.mjs:191:  // Pause, resume, restart; Dev Mode only from Pause; sliders and reset.\ntools/test-flow.mjs:215:    // Live slider: margin changes the running balancer.\ntools/test-flow.mjs:217:    T.tun.margin = 0.9;\ntools/test-flow.mjs:218:    res.sliderLive = g.currentEvent.lanes[0].bal.params.margin * (T.tun.margin / 0.45) !== before;\ntools/test-flow.mjs:219:    T.resetTuning();\ntools/test-flow.mjs:220:    res.resetOK = T.tun.margin === 0.45;\ntools/test-flow.mjs:248:  ok(pd.sliderLive && pd.resetOK, 'a slider changes the running event, reset restores it');\ntools/test-flow.mjs:316:    T.resetTuning();\ntools/test.mjs:210:    T.tun.recoverTime = 0.4;\ntools/test.mjs:220:    T.resetTuning();\n--- plan: bot skill and measured scores\n5:**How to read the numbers.** ✔ means I ran it on this computer on 2026-11-04 with three@0.180.0 and @dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3 and it behaved as described. Skill results are written sharp / average / clumsy, from the calibrated bots in section 17. They\n30:| Absurd little games between the earnest ones | Fruit Hat, Springboard, Tippy Raft |\n83:- **Keys when you're moving, not balancing: direct.** Walking on the island, Tippy Raft, steering in Island Loop and spinning in Springboard's air use the raw key direction, as PC players expect. Plate Spinners has its own scheme ✔, below.\n86:- **Read mouse buttons from the `buttons` bitmask ✔.** Pointer Events don't fire `pointerdown` for a second button while one is already held, so with left and right as the two feet, \"both buttons\" (Hop, Log Reps, Springboard) never registers if you only lis\n195:| 4 | A Little Damp | Quick Lean, One-Foot Hold, Stand Still | Springboard, Still Water, Island Loop | Air control. Group Class invitation |\n196:| 5 | Level Day | Your three best tests | Tippy Raft, Tug of Peace, The Grand Hold | The ending |\n216:**Medals** come from form (0 to 100): ≥40 Adequate, ≥65 Pleasant, ≥85 Exemplary, ≥97 Suspicious. Below 40 is still a pass (\"Attended\"). Section 6 gives an event's form where it has its own formula. Everywhere else, form = 100 × raw / `par`, with `par` set \n280:- *What that gives ✔:* Tier 1: everyone wins with the stick at .9, in 25-48 s. Tier 2: .85 is safe but slow (wins 100% / 88% / 0%); full stick also wins, with 3-4 falls. Tier 3: .85 only wins for the sharp bot; .95 wins 100% / 88% / 0%; full stick means 6-\n311:- *What I measured on Tier 1 ✔:* a sharp bot banking at 7 banks about 28 fruit with no falls. **The same bot never banking falls twice a minute.** A clumsy bot banking at 5 banks 25-30 with no falls; banking at 9 it sometimes falls. That is the whole desig\n320:**Springboard** (the toy-block dive tower at the end of the pier; side camera, slow-mo side replay)\n329:**Tippy Raft** (a round raft at sea; high wide camera; party event) — the one event where players physically fight, and Group Class's reason to exist.\n331:- *Numbers ✔:* radius 6, losing 1 m every 12 s down to 2. Tilt model K 6, C 3.5, 14° for one doll at the rim, clamped to 26°. Slope push `tilt × 10`. Walk 3 m/s. Swell about every 6 s: adds 2.5 rad/s to the tilt velocity. Shove: within 1.3 m, gives the tar\n341:### Island physics (hub, Island Loop, Tippy Raft, finale) ✔\n511:| Circus Green | 0, 2 | Plate Spinners | Pier | 15, 12, running out to sea | Fruit Hat, Plank & Perch, Springboard tower at its end |\n516:| Gazebo | 14, −11 | Group Class, Tippy Raft's dock | | | |\n557:| Balance | Fruit Hat, Room Service, Springboard, Raft | 118 BPM bouncy; marimba, pizzicato, woodblock, tuba-like bass | C6 Am7 Dm7 G7 |\n590:From the main menu or the Gazebo. **Lobby:** four mats. Each pad's Cross joins it, Enter or a click joins keyboard and mouse as one player, Circle or Esc leaves. Seats use the hub's colours. The first to join drives menus. **Playlist:** Quick Class (three \n632:3. **The round runs on `AIHub.time()` alone,** so everyone is in the same class at the same moment. Count down from 3 while the time is negative. Three slots picked with `AIHub.rng('deal')` from the session set (Poses, Cairn, Log Reps, Step Class, Plate Sp\n646:After 10 s with no input on the Title or Main menu, start a loop of bot-played vignettes, about 18 s each, using the real events with bot lanes and god mode on: island walk with the island tipping, Fruit Hat (a greedy bot that topples), The Cairn, Step Cla\n776:- `bot(skill | null)`: `sharp`, `average`, `clumsy` play through the real input path: they write to the stubbed gamepad, not into the game's state.\n786:| sharp | .16 s | 1.4 | .7 | 0 | .12 s | .3 | 28 ms |\n788:| clumsy | .38 s | .8 | .45 | .07 | .5 s | 1.4 | 95 ms |\n798:*events:* for each event and tier, with the sharp bot: it completes, the result is valid, no NaN in any body, bodies return to the baseline count after `dispose()`, a forced fall ragdolls and recovers. One run with rendering on for each event for 2 s with \n800:*balance:* run bots over 3 seeds per event at Tier 1 and assert: sharp reaches Exemplary (≥85) on average, average reaches Pleasant or Adequate, clumsy reaches at least Adequate (≥40), and a bot that parks the stick exactly on the goal and never corrects s\n802:*input:* every verb from the pad stub, from keys, from the mouse, same game effect. Prompts switch the same frame (read `data-glyph`). Xbox glyph option. Menus fully navigable by pad alone, by keyboard alone, by mouse alone. Hover moves the focus. Clicks a\n823:| 3 | The programme | Check-In, Wobble Age, Jar, Today's Plan, days. **Tier A events:** Poses, Log Reps, Step Class, The Cairn, Room Service, Plate Spinners, Springboard |\n824:| 4 | The features | Attract, Dev Mode, Group Class, Tippy Raft, hub session, touch-only, About. Passing the hub harness |\n949:**Every event's numbers were simulated with the bots,** on real Rapier where physics matter: Fruit Hat, Poses, The Cairn, Still Water, Log Reps, Plank & Perch, Tug of Peace, Room Service, Springboard, Island Loop, The Grand Hold and Step Class on the real \n1034:2. *How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?* 13: ground contact capping lean; a parked stick scoring 100%; Plate Spinners unlosable; Plate Spinners unreachable on keys; Tug of Peace unwinnable; Tippy Raft never ending; Lean Match imp\n--- balance checks in tools\n141:        T.bot('sharp');\n188:      T.bot('sharp');\n212:    T.bot('sharp');\n278:      T.bot('sharp');\n397:    for (const skill of ['sharp', 'average', 'clumsy']) {\n404:      ok(results[id].sharp >= 85, `${id} Tier 1 sharp reaches Exemplary`, results[id].sharp.toFixed(0));\n406:      ok(results[id].clumsy >= 40, `${id} Tier 1 clumsy reaches Adequate`, results[id].clumsy.toFixed(0));\n410:  const park = await play('poses', 'sharp', 1, { parkStick: true, noBreath: true });\n412:  const fh = await play('fruitHat', 'sharp', 1, { bankAt: 7 });\n413:  ok(fh.falls === 0, 'Fruit Hat Tier 1: sharp banking at 7 has no falls', String(fh.falls));\n414:  const never = await play('fruitHat', 'sharp', 1, { bankAt: 999 });\n416:  const pl = [await play('plates', 'sharp', 1), await play('plates', 'sharp', 2)];\n417:  const ps = [await play('plates', 'clumsy', 1), await play('plates', 'clumsy', 2)];\n502:      for (const skill of ['sharp', 'average', 'clumsy']) {\n506:        if (id === 'roomService' && skill === 'sharp') ok(rs.every((x) => x.glasses >= 4), `Room Service on ${device} delivers`, rs.map((x) => x.glasses).join(','));\n508:      info(device, id, Object.entries(row).map(([k, v]) => `${k} ${v.toFixed(0)}`).join(' '), 'stick', ['sharp', 'average', 'clumsy'].map((k) => results[id][k].toFixed(0)).join('/'));\n509:      ok(row.sharp >= 60, `${id} on ${device}: sharp gets a good score`, row.sharp.toFixed(0));\n510:      ok(row.sharp >= results[id].sharp - 30, `${id} on ${device} holds up against the stick`, `${row.sharp.toFixed(0)} vs ${results[id].sharp.toFixed(0)}`);\n511:      // Still Water's small zone makes a delayed bot oscillate. The plan measured its clumsy bot at 24-28% in the zone: keep a floor, not a medal.\n512:      ok(row.clumsy >= (id === 'stillWater' ? 10 : 20), `${id} on ${device}: clumsy still gets somewhere`, row.clumsy.toFixed(0));\n514:    const fall = await viaDevice(device, 'fruitHat', 'sharp', 1, { bankAt: 7 });\n515:    ok(fall.falls === 0, `Fruit Hat on ${device}: sharp banking at 7 has no falls`, String(fall.falls));\n517:  const mp = await viaDevice('mouse', 'plates', 'sharp', 1), mc = await viaDevice('mouse', 'plates', 'clumsy', 1);\n520:  // The Check-In: every test gives the sharp bot a fair score. Lean Match was impossible in the plan's first version.\n531:      T.bot('sharp');\n542:  for (const k of ['standStill', 'leanMatch', 'quickLean', 'oneFoot', 'stepTime']) ok((checkin[k] ?? 0) > 0.3, `Check-In ${k} scores above .3 for the sharp bot`, String(checkin[k]));\n543:  const tug = await play('tug', 'sharp', 1);\n545:  const log = await play('logReps', 'clumsy', 1);\n546:  ok(log.form <= 75, 'Log Reps does not hand the clumsy bot too much', log.form.toFixed(0));\n547:  const rs = await play('roomService', 'sharp', 1);\n549:  const cs = await play('cairn', 'sharp', 2, { noBreath: false }, 1);\n550:  const cn = await play('cairn', 'sharp', 2, { noBreath: true }, 1);\n--- issues mentioning raft or springboard scores\n5:4. Springboard: base class recovered the ragdoll before the event's water timer did, crashing every dive (\"Cannot read properties of null\"). Fixed: a separate water state.\n6:5. Balance torque kept acting on the core in Springboard's air. Fixed: no ankle torque when released.\n7:6. Tippy Raft rounds too long: slope push was an acceleration rather than a direct push as the plan measured. Fixed.\n9:8. Rapier panic ('unreachable') on Springboard's second dive: a joint re-created on a disabled body. Fixed: enable the body first, then rejoin. Found only by running every dive.\n10:9. God mode's quiet stand-up also fired in Springboard's air, teleporting the diver back to the board mid-flight whenever they spun past 45 degrees. Fixed: no fall checks in the air.\n11:10. Second Rapier panic in Springboard: disabling a free core (setEnabled(false) after its joint was removed) panicked world.step on a later dive, depending on timing. Fixed: the core is parked out\n22:21. Art pass: Tippy Raft's low side sank under the sea at big tilts, hiding half the raft and the dolls on it. Fixed: visual tilt eased and sea lowered.\n33:32. By reading the verbs, not a test: with a mouse, pumping Springboard (both buttons) also launched instantly, because both buttons is Hop. Fixed: launch is Space or the middle button on keyboard \n44:43. Plan audit: Tippy Raft's swells had no visible rising wave, and Plate Spinners' band colour wasn't on the hoop. Fixed.\n47:46. Plan audit: the balance test's three seeds were one seed for any event without random draws, because the bots ignored the seed, so skill separation in Springboard rested on one sample. Fixed.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e","uuid":"ac62bcd2-12cf-4038-9de5-4ef63a5d2846","timestamp":"2026-11-05T15:22:05.479Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"--- slider tests in tools\ntools/test-flow.mjs:191:  // Pause, resume, restart; Dev Mode only from Pause; sliders and reset.\ntools/test-flow.mjs:215:    // Live slider: margin changes the running balancer.\ntools/test-flow.mjs:217:    T.tun.margin = 0.9;\ntools/test-flow.mjs:218:    res.sliderLive = g.currentEvent.lanes[0].bal.params.margin * (T.tun.margin / 0.45) !== before;\ntools/test-flow.mjs:219:    T.resetTuning();\ntools/test-flow.mjs:220:    res.resetOK = T.tun.margin === 0.45;\ntools/test-flow.mjs:248:  ok(pd.sliderLive && pd.resetOK, 'a slider changes the running event, reset restores it');\ntools/test-flow.mjs:316:    T.resetTuning();\ntools/test.mjs:210:    T.tu