events:* for each event and tier, with the sharp bot: it completes, the result is valid, no NaN in any body, bodies return to the baseline count after `dispose()`, a forced fall ragdolls and recovers. One run with rendering on for each event for 2 s with \n800:*balance:* run bots over 3 seeds per event at Tier 1 and assert: sharp reaches Exemplary (≥85) on average, average reaches Pleasant or Adequate, clumsy reaches at least Adequate (≥40), and a bot that parks the stick exactly on the goal and never corrects s\n802:*input:* every verb from the pad stub, from keys, from the mouse, same game effect. Prompts switch the same frame (read `data-glyph`). Xbox glyph option. Menus fully navigable by pad alone, by keyboard alone, by mouse alone. Hover moves the focus. Clicks a\n823:| 3 | The programme | Check-In, Wobble Age, Jar, Today's Plan, days. **Tier A events:** Poses, Log Reps, Step Class, The Cairn, Room Service, Plate Spinners, Springboard |\n824:| 4 | The features | Attract, Dev Mode, Group Class, Tippy Raft, hub session, touch-only, About. Passing the hub harness |\n949:**Every event's numbers were simulated with the bots,** on real Rapier where physics matter: Fruit Hat, Poses, The Cairn, Still Water, Log Reps, Plank & Perch, Tug of Peace, Room Service, Springboard, Island Loop, The Grand Hold and Step Class on the real \n1034:2. *How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?* 13: ground contact capping lean; a parked stick scoring 100%; Plate Spinners unlosable; Plate Spinners unreachable on keys; Tug of Peace unwinnable; Tippy Raft never ending; Lean Match imp\n--- balance checks in tools\n141:        T.bot('sharp');\n188:      T.bot('sharp');\n212:    T.bot('sharp');\n278:      T.bot('sharp');\n397:    for (const skill of ['sharp', 'average', 'clumsy']) {\n404:      ok(results[id].sharp >= 85, `${id} Tier 1 sharp reaches Exemplary`, results[id].sharp.toFixed(0));\n406:      ok(results[id].clumsy >= 40, `${id} Tier 1 clumsy reaches Adequate`, results[id].clumsy.toFixed(0));\n410:  const park = await play('poses', 'sharp', 1, { parkStick: true, noBreath: true });\n412:  const fh = await play('fruitHat', 'sharp', 1, { bankAt: 7 });\n413:  ok(fh.falls === 0, 'Fruit Hat Tier 1: sharp banking at 7 has no falls', String(fh.falls));\n414:  const never = await play('fruitHat', 'sharp', 1, { bankAt: 999 });\n416:  const pl = [await play('plates', 'sharp', 1), await play('plates', 'sharp', 2)];\n417:  const ps = [await play('plates', 'clumsy', 1), await play('plates', 'clumsy', 2)];\n502:      for (const skill of ['sharp', 'average', 'clumsy']) {\n506:        if (id === 'roomService' && skill === 'sharp') ok(rs.every((x) => x.glasses >= 4), `Room Service on ${device} delivers`, rs.map((x) => x.glasses).join(','));\n508:      info(device, id, Object.entries(row).map(([k, v]) => `${k} ${v.toFixed(0)}`).join(' '), 'stick', ['sharp', 'average', 'clumsy'].map((k) => results[id][k].toFixed(0)).join('/'));\n509:      ok(row.sharp >= 60, `${id} on ${device}: sharp gets a good score`, row.sharp.toFixed(0));\n510:      ok(row.sharp >= results[id].sharp - 30, `${id} on ${device} holds up against the stick`, `${row.sharp.toFixed(0)} vs ${results[id].sharp.toFixed(0)}`);\n511:      // Still Water's small zone makes a delayed bot oscillate. The plan measured its clumsy bot at 24-28% in the zone: keep a floor, not a medal.\n512:      ok(row.clumsy >= (id === 'stillWater' ? 10 : 20), `${id} on ${device}: clumsy still gets somewhere`, row.clumsy.toFixed(0));\n514:    const fall = await viaDevice(device, 'fruitHat', 'sharp', 1, { bankAt: 7 });\n515:    ok(fall.falls === 0, `Fruit Hat on ${device}: sharp banking at 7 has no falls`, String(fall.falls));\n517:  const mp = await viaDevice('mouse', 'plates', 'sharp', 1), mc = await viaDevice('mouse', 'plates', 'clumsy', 1);\n520:  // The Check-In: every test gives the sharp bot a fair score. Lean Match was impossible in the plan's first version.\n531:      T.bot('sharp');\n542:  for (const k of ['standStill', 'leanMatch', 'quickLean', 'oneFoot', 'stepTime']) ok((checkin[k] ?? 0) > 0.3, `Check-In ${k} scores above .3 for the sharp bot`, String(checkin[k]));\n543:  const tug = await play('tug', 'sharp', 1);\n545:  const log = await play('logReps', 'clumsy', 1);\n546:  ok(log.form <= 75, 'Log Reps does not hand the clumsy bot too much', log.form.toFixed(0));\n547:  const rs = await play('roomService', 'sharp', 1);\n549:  const cs = await play('cairn', 'sharp', 2, { noBreath: false }, 1);\n550:  const cn = await play('cairn', 'sharp', 2, { noBreath: true }, 1);\n--- issues mentioning raft or springboard scores\n5:4. Springboard: base class recovered the ragdoll before the event's water timer did, crashing every dive (\"Cannot read properties of null\"). Fixed: a separate water state.\n6:5. Balance torque kept acting on the core in Springboard's air. Fixed: no ankle torque when released.\n7:6. Tippy Raft rounds too long: slope push was an acceleration rather than a direct push as the plan measured. Fixed.\n9:8. Rapier panic ('unreachable') on Springboard's second dive: a joint re-created on a disabled body. Fixed: enable the body first, then rejoin. Found only by running every dive.\n10:9. God mode's quiet stand-up also fired in Springboard's air, teleporting the diver back to the board mid-flight whenever they spun past 45 degrees. Fixed: no fall checks in the air.\n11:10. Second Rapier panic in Springboard: disabling a free core (setEnabled(false) after its joint was removed) panicked world.step on a later dive, depending on timing. Fixed: the core is parked out\n22:21. Art pass: Tippy Raft's low side sank under the sea at big tilts, hiding half the raft and the dolls on it. Fixed: visual tilt eased and sea lowered.\n33:32. By reading the verbs, not a test: with a mouse, pumping Springboard (both buttons) also launched instantly, because both buttons is Hop. Fixed: launch is Space or the middle button on keyboard \n44:43. Plan audit: Tippy Raft's swells had no visible rising wave, and Plate Spinners' band colour wasn't on the hoop. Fixed.\n47:46. Plan audit: the balance test's three seeds were one seed for any event without random draws, because the bots ignored the seed, so skill separation in Springboard rested on one sample. Fixed.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011kkJHir3vrY674JD4Fh56W","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
