{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NwoaHaPRDV39ozC4EBSCBN","type":"tool_result","content":"free GB 3\n296 passed, 0 failed\n--- current hand-in text on testing\ntesting: Allowed: as much headless testing as wanted, scripts that play the game and check its state including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, one command printing only failures and a one-line count, screenshots only for what a script can't check, no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Ran: node tools/test.mjs with eight groups and about 2,035 checks: whole-game playthrough by bots on a stubbed pad, every event and tier, balance tables over three seeds, the same bots again through real key and pointer events, every verb on pad, keys and mouse, offline audio renders, the hub harness at 1, 2 and 4 players, bad network and host leaving, the 1080p layout audit, touch profiles, a WebGL2 boot in WebKit, plus a screenshot art pass. Not run: real controller, real TV, human ears, a human player.\n1 49 logged in notes/issues.md as they happened: 38 caught by test scripts, measurements and screenshots, 11 found by reading code paths and by checking the build line by line against the plan.\n2 11: Hop presses lost during hit-stop, every Tug of Peace doll falling, the Springboard crash, two Rapier panics on later dives, divers teleporting in mid-air, the game stuck at the first Wobble Age, the finale's doll hidden inside the lamp, Step Class footprints hidden behind the doll, Trudy's lean tutorial being impossible, and Enter on the session card missing the hub's time limit under load, which would have kept the game out of sessions.\n3 The scripted whole-game playthrough with bots on a stubbed pad. It got stuck on real flow bugs no single event test could show, including the first Wobble Age and the lean tutorial, and it runs the whole game in about a minute of machine time. Running the same bots through real keys and mouse came second: it found Log Reps unfair on keys, late in the build.\n4 The per-event rendered smoke run and the WebKit boot. Both passed the first time and changed nothing, though they remain worth keeping as guards.\n47. Long headless runs: sound nodes piled up because the sim runs about 170x real time, reaching 981 MB and making my browser earlyoom's target. Not a leak in p\n48. Screenshot: the finale's bedsheet catch and the ending's marble flare both happened off camera. Fixed: the camera follows the fall to a sheet held by the cl\n49. Screenshot: marbles were white in normal play. The jar's mesh first drew with no colour attribute, on the title, and stayed white for good, so medal colours\n8:- Issue log: `notes/issues.md` in the dev folder (49 issues)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e","uuid":"1290f0a4-2fce-44c5-a1cb-479690c38fc3","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:01:18.330Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"free GB 3\n296 passed, 0 failed\n--- current hand-in text on testing\ntesting: Allowed: as much headless testing as wanted, scripts that play the game and check its state including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, one command printing only failures and a one-line count, screenshots only for what a script can't check, no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Ran: node tools/test.mjs with eight groups and about 2,035 checks: whole-game playthrough by bots on a stubbed pad, every event and tier, balance tables over three seeds, the same bots again through real key and pointer events, every verb on pad, keys and mouse, offline audio renders, the hub harness at 1, 2 and 4 players, bad network and host leaving, the 1080p layout audit, touch profiles, a WebGL2 boot in WebKit, plus a screenshot art pass. Not run: real controller, real TV, human ears, a human player.\n1 49 logged in notes/issues.md as they happened: 38 caught by test scripts, measurements and screenshots, 11 found by reading code paths and by checking the build line by line against the plan.\n2 11: Hop presses lost during hit-stop, every Tug of Peace doll falling, the Springboard crash, two Rapier panics on later dives, divers teleporting in mid-air, the game stuck at the first Wobble Age, the finale's doll hidden inside the lamp, Step Class footprints hidden behind the doll, Trudy's lean tutorial being impossible, and Enter on the session card missing the hub's time limit under load, which would have kept the game out of sessions.\n3 The scripted whole-game playthrough with bots on a stubbed pad. It got stuck on real flow bugs no single event test could show, including the first Wobble Age and the lean tutorial, and it runs the whole game in about a minute of machine time. Running the same bots through real keys and mouse came second: it found Log Reps unfair on keys, late in the build.\n4 The per-event rendered smoke run and the WebKit boot. Both passed the first time and changed nothing, though they remain worth keeping as guards.\n47. Long headless runs: sound nodes piled up because the sim runs about 170x real time, reaching 981 MB and making my browser earlyoom's target. Not a leak in p\n48. Screenshot: the finale's bedsheet catch and the ending's marble flare both happened off camera. Fixed: the camera follows the fall to a sheet held by the cl\n49. Screenshot: marbles were white in normal play. The jar's mesh first drew with no colour attribute, on the title, and stayed white for good, so medal colours\n8:- Issue log: `notes/issues.md` in the dev folder (49 issues)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NwoaHaPRDV39ozC4EBSCBN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
