{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgk4VuP52YMRejHeNiK8d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XFFgqCuXdh4mPh8edhP922","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n \"2,035\\|2035\\|49 logged\\|49 issues\" -r tools src/data/aboutPages.js ../PROGRESS.md notes/hub-README.md | cut -c1-150; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='notes/issues.md'; s=open(p).read().rstrip('\\n')\ns+='''\n50. By reading the test, while checking the plan line by line: the Dev Mode slider test could never fail. It compared a value with itself times a ratio, not what the game did, so \"a slider changes the running event\" proved nothing. Replaced with tools/test-sliders.mjs: every slider moved while the game runs and judged by what the game then does, the d-pad, mouse and reset through the real screen, and the ink sliders read back from the picture.\n51. The new slider test: Island rest tilt did nothing until something else happened to sync the island. Fixed: the slider and Reset tuning both sync it.\n52. Measurement, dive by dive: every skill reached the same board speed and height, because the board's simulated position was clamped at .7 m, which holds a spring of this period near 4.9 m/s. The plan's 6.5 and 7.6 m/s after 5 and 7 s of pumping were out of reach and pumping longer earned nothing. Fixed: the spring runs free and only what you see stops at .7 m. Now 4.8 / 6.5 / 7.5 at .07 s late, 3.4 / 4.6 / 5.2 at .14 s late, 1.5 a quarter period late, against the plan's 4.7 / 6.5 / 7.6, 3.6 / 4.6 / 5.2 and 1.5.\n53. Same measurement: the Springboard bot's reaction lag was only a small speed threshold, not a delay, so all skills pumped alike. Fixed: real lateness, and a shorter pump. Launch 5.7 / 3.6 / 3.0 m/s and height 6.7 / 5.7 / 5.4 m, against the plan's 5.4 / 3.8 / 3 and 6.5 / 5.7 / 5.5.\n54. Same measurement: the Springboard bot sometimes tried head first at half stick from the 5 m tower, which the plan measured at 0% for everyone, and scored 8 for it. Fixed: a bot only tries what it can reach in its air time.\n55. The new framing test: once a long pump paid off again, the diver left the top of the fixed camera's picture. Fixed: the camera rises with the highest diver and is back down for the splash.\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='../exit-interview.json'; t=open(p).read()\niv=json.loads(t)\nold1=iv['testingFeedback'][0]; new1='55 logged in notes/issues.md as they happened: 43 caught by test scripts, measurements and screenshots, 12 found by reading code paths and by checking the build line by line against the plan.'\nold4=iv['testingFeedback'][3]; new4='The Dev Mode slider test as I first wrote it. It compared a number with itself, so it could never fail, and it stood in front of a slider that really did nothing until I replaced it with one that measures every slider in the running game. Among tests that could fail, the per-event rendered smoke run and the WebKit boot passed the first time and changed nothing, though they remain worth keeping as guards.'\nassert old1 in t and old4 in t and 'about 2,035 checks' in t\nt=t.replace(old1,new1).replace(old4,new4).replace('about 2,035 checks','about 2,090 checks')\njson.loads(t); open(p,'w').write(t)\n\np='../PROGRESS.md'; s=open(p).read()\nassert '(49 issues)' in s\ns=s.replace('(49 issues)','(55 issues)')\ns=s.rstrip('\\n')+'''\n\n## Last pass\nChecking the plan line by line showed the slider test could never fail. Replacing it, and re-measuring Springboard, found issues 50-55 (see the log). Fixed: Island rest tilt, the board's clamp, the Springboard bot, the camera on high dives. `tools/test-sliders.mjs` is new and runs in the flow group.\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs >/dev/null 2>&1; echo build $?; sha256sum ../WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442.html | cut -c1-16; python3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print('interview parses')\"","description":"Log issues, update hand-ins, rebuild the final file"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2157,"cache_read_input_tokens":183103,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2157},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e","uuid":"9648e6cc-b1a7-45a7-94b3-29fe2a721c02","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:01:49.576Z","request_id":"req_011Cgk4Vu3EP8Tp5oXTSH399","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XFFgqCuXdh4mPh8edhP922":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-044442__x29b4d9/work/WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442 && grep -n \"2,035\\|2035\\|49 logged\\|49 issues\" -r tools src/data/aboutPages.js ../PROGRESS.md notes/hub-README.md | cut -c1-150; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='notes/issues.md'; s=open(p).read().rstrip('\\n')\ns+='''\n50. By reading the test, while checking the plan line by line: the Dev Mode slider test could never fail. It compared a value with itself times a ratio, not what the game did, so \"a slider changes the running event\" proved nothing. Replaced with tools/test-sliders.mjs: every slider moved while the game runs and judged by what the game then does, the d-pad, mouse and reset through the real screen, and the ink sliders read back from the picture.\n51. The new slider test: Island rest tilt did nothing until something else happened to sync the island. Fixed: the slider and Reset tuning both sync it.\n52. Measurement, dive by dive: every skill reached the same board speed and height, because the board's simulated position was clamped at .7 m, which holds a spring of this period near 4.9 m/s. The plan's 6.5 and 7.6 m/s after 5 and 7 s of pumping were out of reach and