{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkB8vosebfewbAcdFtFy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Flow and balance both pass now (229 of 229), and the playthrough reaches the ending again. Still Water's bot scores 33 on keys and 61 on mouse, up from the 12–16 I'd flagged as weak, since the harness caused part of that. Next I'll record the issues and corrected hand-ins, run two last plan checks, then do the final full run with its output saved as evidence.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4731,"cache_read_input_tokens":496759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4731},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e","uuid":"439a8a9e-736e-4861-aa82-dbc0a4d21c07","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:28:56.652Z","request_id":"req_011CgkB8vXko1ogwotreXKCF","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":4,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkB8vosebfewbAcdFtFy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0162ghDYSv8BHHJKRFSrHG9A","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n \"ringX\\|1\\.6\\|recentre\\|KeyC\" tools/test-input.mjs | cut -c1-130 | head -5; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='notes/issues.md'; s=open(p).read().rstrip('\\n')\ns+='''\n56. Playing every figure in the plan against the build: the island walker fell through the ground from the moment it arrived, and kept falling, because the ground's filter leaves out doll bits and the walker is a doll. It never touched the fence or a prop, and you could walk straight off the island and out over the sea, to radius 50 and beyond. Every earlier check read x and z only. Critical. Fixed: the disc and fence stop everything on the island.\n57. Same pass: Tug of Peace was close to unwinnable above Tier 1, 0% for everyone on Tier 3. The ease-off's hit fired again on every step of its .8 s, and the lean grows during it, so the plan's safe .85 fell 14-19 times. Critical. Fixed: one hit, at the moment they ease off.\n58. Same pass: a fall in Tug also let the rope run against you while you lay there, on top of its leap, so full stick could never win. Fixed: the leap is the cost, and nobody hauls while one side is on the floor.\n59. Same pass: Room Service had lost its lesson. My fix for issue 7 softened the side step so far that not bracing cost nothing. Fixed: a named rate, 70 /s, swept against the plan's glass counts.\n60. Same pass: Gary swooping every 13 s was my own number, and with spills back it emptied Tier 3 for everyone. Fixed: once at 14 s, then every 26 s.\n61. The playthrough, after the Raft bots changed: two bots on one spot could not shove each other, and the raft stops shrinking at radius 1, so a round could run for ever with a player already in the water. It only ever ended by luck. Critical. Fixed: a point blank shove has full strength, and every round ends within 90 s.\n62. Same pass: Quick Lean's next prompt did not wait for the dot to come back, so a repeated direction scored as an instant reaction and the slowest bot beat the fastest. Fixed, and reaction now reads the first .15 of lean, which is what the score's .35 s stands for.\n63. Same pass: Step Class charts were too dense. Tier 2 had 112 notes for the plan's 108, Tier 3 had 153 for 126, the session 53 foot and 11 lean for 54 and 10. Fixed by swapping bars.\n64. Same pass: pars were not putting the sharp bot at 88 to 95. Set again for The Cairn, Plank, Island Loop, Fruit Hat, Room Service and Springboard, once the bots below were right.\n65. Same pass: the bots' timing error had .575 of the spread in the plan's table, so every timed skill read too good. Fixed.\n66. Same pass: the stick's dead zone swallowed the pad bots' noise and small corrections. Fixed in the test hook: they aim past it, as a person does.\n67. Same pass: the bots' hand noise sat on the doll's resonance and collapsed the clumsy bot. The plan does not say its frequency. Swept against Still Water and Poses, and set to 2 and 1.65 rad/s.\n68. Same pass: in the Grand Hold the sharp bot's gain oscillated at that stiffness, as the plan warned, scoring 0% in the last ring while the clumsy bot scored 94%. Fixed: the under-load gain.\n69. Same pass: the Fruit Hat bot's feedback whipped it past every fruit, the plan's other warning. Fixed: a plain push .95 s before landing, and an earlier flail. Banked 26 and 30, against the plan's 28 and 25-30.\n70. Same pass: the Tug bot pushed past its stick setting and its late presses were clamped to on time, so clumsy won what it should lose. Fixed.\n71. Same pass: the Raft bots played too carefully, with rounds averaging 50 s and clumsy never winning. Retuned to the plan's measured rounds and wins.\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='../exit-interview.json'; t=open(p).read(); iv=json.loads(t)\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global t\n    assert old in t, old[:60]; t=t.replace(old,new)\nrep(iv['testingFeedback'][0],'71 logged in notes/issues.md as they happened: 59 caught by test scripts, measurements and screenshots, 12 found by reading code paths and by checking the build line by line against the plan.')\nrep(iv['testingFeedback'][1],\"14: Hop presses lost during hit-stop, every Tug of Peace doll falling, the Springboard crash, two Rapier panics on later dives, divers teleporting in mid-air, the game stuck at the first Wobble Age, the finale's doll hidden inside the lamp, Step Class footprints hidden behind the doll, Trudy's lean tutorial being impossible, Enter on the session card missing the hub's time limit under load, which would have kept the game out of sessions, the island walker falling through the ground so you could walk out over the sea, Tug of Peace close to unwinnable above Tier 1, and a Tippy Raft round that could run for ever.\")\nrep(iv['testingFeedback'][2],'The scripted whole-game playthrough with bots on a stubbed pad. It got stuck on real flow bugs no single event test could show, including the first Wobble Age and the lean tutorial, and it runs the whole game in about a minute of machine time. Close behind, and I should have run it far sooner: playing every figure PLAN.md measured against the finished build. With about 2,000 other checks passing, it found the walker falling through the island, Tug of Peace close to unwinnable and Room Service without its lesson.')\nrep(iv['engineFeedback'][1],iv['engineFeedback'][1]+' And my own collision filter let the island walker fall through the ground for most of the build: nothing read its height, so nothing showed it.')\nrep('with eight groups and about 2,090 checks','with nine groups and about 2,360 checks')\nrep('every event and tier, balance tables over three seeds,','every event and tier, balance tables over three seeds, every figure PLAN.md measured played against the build,')\njson.loads(t); open(p,'w').write(t)\n\np='../PROGRESS.md'; s=open(p).read()\nassert '(55 issues)' in s; s=s.replace('(55 issues)','(71 issues)')\na=s.index('## Last pass')\ns=s[:a]+'''## Last pass\nChecking the plan line by line showed the slider test could never fail, and re-measuring Springboard showed a clamp the earlier audit had missed. So every figure the plan measured was played against the build: issues 50-71 in the log. `tools/test-sliders.mjs` runs in the flow group and `tools/test-plan.mjs` is the new plan group. `notes/plan-figures.txt` holds the last run's numbers.\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='tools/test-plan.mjs'; s=open(p).read()\nold=\"  // Plank & Perch: these bots hold the zone better\"\nnew=\"\"\"  // The log is a rule, not a contact: past 6 degrees it creeps, and at .5 m it goes.\n  const log = await page.evaluate(() => {\n    const T = window.__TEST__, g = T.game, STEP = 1 / 120;\n    T.startEvent('logReps', 0, {});\n    const ev = g.currentEvent, l = ev.lanes[0];\n    for (let n = 0; ev.phase !== 'play' && n < 400; n++) T.advance(0.05);\n    T.advance(0.5);\n    const was = l.offset;\n    T.stick(0.2, 0); T.advance(1);\n    const small = Math.abs(l.offset - was);\n    T.stick(1, 0);\n    let t = 0;\n    while (t < 6 && !l.logLost) { T.advance(STEP); t += STEP; }\n    T.stick(0, 0);\n    const o = { small, t, lost: l.logLost };\n    T.goto('menu');\n    return o;\n  });\n  ok(log.small < 0.1, 'Log Reps: a small lean hardly moves the log', log.small.toFixed(3));\n  ok(log.lost && log.t < 3, 'Log Reps: a big lean drops the log', log.t.toFixed(2));\n  // Keys in balance events move the asking ring, at 1.6 units a second, and it stays where you leave it.\n  const ring = await page.evaluate(() => {\n    const T = window.__TEST__, g = T.game;\n    T.startEvent('poses', 0, {});\n    const ev = g.currentEvent;\n    for (let n = 0; ev.phase !== 'play' && n < 400; n++) T.advance(0.05);\n    const key = (code, on) => window.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent(on ? 'keydown' : 'keyup', { code, key: code }));\n    key('KeyC', true); T.advance(0.02); key('KeyC', false); T.advance(0.02);\n    const from = g.input.ringX;\n    key('KeyD', true); T.advance(0.25); key('KeyD', false); T.advance(0.02);\n    const moved = g.input.ringX - from;\n    T.advance(1);\n    const kept = g.input.ringX - from;\n    key('KeyC', true); T.advance(0.02); key('KeyC', false); T.advance(0.02);\n    const back = g.input.ringX;\n    T.goto('menu');\n    return { moved, kept, back };\n  });\n  near('holding a key moves the ring, in .25 s', ring.moved, 0.4, 0.04);\n  ok(Math.abs(ring.kept - ring.moved) < 0.001, 'the ring stays where you leave it', ring.kept.toFixed(3));\n  ok(ring.back === 0, 'C recentres the ring', String(ring.back));\n  await fresh();\n\n  // Plank & Perch: these bots hold the zone better\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 2p notes/issues.md | cut -c1-60; python3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print('interview parses')\"; node tools/build.mjs >/dev/null 2>&1; echo build $?; rm -rf notes/scratch; H=../WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442.html; sha256sum $H | cut -c1-16","description":"Log issues, update hand-ins, add last checks, rebuild"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4731,"cache_read_input_tokens":496759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4731},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e","uuid":"21a01dbc-2019-40bb-8e2c-e6bb5ce975fd","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:29:26.349Z","request_id":"req_011CgkB8vXko1ogwotreXKCF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0162ghDYSv8BHHJKRFSrHG9A":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-044442__x29b4d9/work/WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442 && grep -n \"ringX\\|1\\.6\\|recentre\\|KeyC\" tools/test-input.mjs | cut -c1-130 | head -5; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='notes/issues.md'; s=open(p).read().rstrip('\\n')\ns+='''\n56. Playing every figure in the plan against the build: the island walker fell through the ground from the moment it arrived, and kept falling, because the ground's filter leaves out doll bits and the walker is a doll. It never touched the fence or a prop, and you could walk straight off the island and out over the sea, to radius 50 and beyond. Every earlier check read x and z only. Critical. Fixed: the disc and fence stop everything on the island.\n57. Same pass: Tug of Peace was close to unwinnable above Tier 1, 0% for everyone on Tier 3. The ease-off's hit fired again on every step of its .8 s, and the lean grows during it, so the plan's safe .85 fell 14-19 times. Critical. Fixed: one hit, at the moment they ease off.\n58. Same pass: a fall in Tug also let the rope run against you while you lay there, on top of its leap, so full stick could never win. Fixed: the leap is the cost, and nobody hauls while one side is on the floor.\n59. Same pass: Room Service had lost its lesson. My fix for issue 7 softened the side step so far that not bracing cost nothing. Fixed: a named rate, 70 /s, swept against the plan's glass counts.\n60. Same pass: Gary swooping every 13 s was my own number, and with spills back it emptied Tier 3 for everyone. Fixed: once at 14 s, then every 26 s.\n61. The playthrough, after the Raft bots changed: two bots on one spot could not shove each other, and the raft stops shrinking at radius 1, so a round could run for ever with a player already in the water. It only ever ended by luck. Critical. Fixed: a point blank shove has full strength, and every round ends within 90 s.\n62. Same pass: Quick Lean's next prompt did not wait for the dot to come back, so a repeated direction scored as an instant reaction and the slowest bot beat the fastest. Fixed, and reaction now reads the first .15 of lean, which is what the score's .35 s stands for.\n63. Same pass: Step Class charts were too dense. Tier 2 had 112 notes for the plan's 108, Tier 3 had 153 for 126, the session 53 foot and 11 lean for 54 and 10. Fixed by swapping bars.\n64. Same pass: pars were not putting the sharp bot at 88 to 95. Set again for The Cairn, Plank, Island Loop, Fruit Hat, Room Service and Springboard, once the bots below were right.\n65. Same pass: the bots' timing error had .575 of the spread in the plan's table, so every timed skill read too good. Fixed.\n66. Same pass: the stick's dead zone swallowed the pad bots' noise and small corrections. Fixed in the test hook: they aim past it, as a person does.\n67. Same pass: the bots' hand noise sat on the doll's resonance and collapsed the clumsy bot. The plan does not say its frequency. Swept against Still Water and Poses, and set to 2 and 1.65 rad/s.\n68. Same pass: in the Grand Hold the sharp bot's gain oscillated at that stiffness, as the plan warned, scoring 0% in the last ring while the clumsy bot scored 94%. Fixed: the under-load gain.\n69. Same pass: the Fruit Hat bot's feedback whipped it past every fruit, the plan's other warning. Fixed: a plain push .95 s before landing, and an earlier flail. Banked 26 and 30, against the plan's 28 and 25-30.\n70. Same pass: the Tug bot pushed past its stick setting and its late presses were clamped to on time, so clumsy won what it should lose. Fixed.\n71. Same pass: the Raft bots played too carefully, with rounds averaging 50 s and clumsy never winning. Retuned to the plan's measured rounds and wins.\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='../exit-interview.json'; t=open(p).read(); iv=json.loads(t)\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global t\n    assert old in t, old[:60]; t=t.replace(old,new)\nrep(iv['testingFeedback'][0],'71 logged in notes/issues.md as they happened: 59 caught by test scripts, measurements and screenshots, 12 found by reading code paths and by checking the build line by line against the plan.')\nrep(iv['testingFeedback'][1],\"14: Hop presses lost during hit-stop, every Tug of Peace doll falling, the Springboard crash, two Rapier panics on later dives, divers teleporting in mid-air, the game stuck at the first Wobble Age, the finale's doll hidden inside the lamp, Step Class footprints hidden behind the doll, Trudy's lean tutorial being impossible, Enter on the session card missing the hub's time limit under load, which would have kept the game out of sessions, the island walker falling through the ground so you could walk out over the sea, Tug of Peace close to unwinnable above Tier 1, and a Tippy Raft round that could run for ever.\")\nrep(iv['testingFeedback'][2],'The scripted whole-game playthrough with bots on a stubbed pad. It got stuck on real flow bugs no single event test could show, including the first Wobble Age and the lean tutorial, and it runs the whole game in about a minute of machine time. Close behind, and I should have run it far sooner: playing every figure PLAN.md measured against the finished build. With about 2,000 other checks passing, it found the walker falling through the island, Tug of Peace close to unwinnable and Room Service without its lesson.')\nrep(iv['engineFeedback'][1],iv['engineFeedback'][1]+' And my own collision filter let the island walker fall through the ground for most of the build: nothing read its height, so nothing showed it.')\nrep('with eight groups and about 2,090 checks','with nine groups and about 2,360 checks')\nrep('every event and tier, balance tables over three seeds,','every event and tier, balance tables over three seeds, every figure PLAN.md measured played against the build,')\njson.loads(t); open(p,'w').write(t)\n\np='../PROGRESS.md'; s=open(p).read()\nassert '(55 issues)' in s; s=s.replace('(55 issues)','(71 issues)')\na=s.index('## Last pass')\ns=s[:a]+'''## Last pass\nChecking the plan line by line showed the slider test could never fail, and re-measuring Springboard showed a clamp the earlier audit had missed. So every figure the plan measured was played against the build: issues 50-71 in the log. `tools/test-sliders.mjs` runs in the flow group and `tools/test-plan.mjs` is the new plan group. `notes/plan-figures.txt` holds the last run's numbers.\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='tools/test-plan.mjs'; s=open(p).read()\nold=\"  // Plank & Perch: these bots hold the zone better\"\nnew=\"\"\"  // The log is a rule, not a contact: past 6 degrees it creeps, and at .5 m it goes.\n  const log = await page.evaluate(() => {\n    const T = window.__TEST__, g = T.game, STEP = 1 / 120;\n    T.startEvent('logReps', 0, {});\n    const ev = g.currentEvent, l = ev.lanes[0];\n    for (let n = 0; ev.phase !== 'play' && n < 400; n++) T.advance(0.05);\n    T.advance(0.5);\n    const was = l.offset;\n    T.stick(0.2, 0); T.advance(1);\n    const small = Math.abs(l.offset - was);\n    T.stick(1, 0);\n    let t = 0;\n    while (t < 6 && !l.logLost) { T.advance(STEP); t += STEP; }\n    T.stick(0, 0);\n    const o = { small, t, lost: l.logLost };\n    T.goto('menu');\n    return o;\n  });\n  ok(log.small < 0.1, 'Log Reps: a small lean hardly moves the log', log.small.toFixed(3));\n  ok(log.lost && log.t < 3, 'Log Reps: a big lean drops the log', log.t.toFixed(2));\n  // Keys in balance events move the asking ring, at 1.6 units a second, and it stays where you leave it.\n  const ring = await page.evaluate(() => {\n    const T = window.__TEST__, g = T.game;\n    T.startEvent('poses', 0, {});\n    const ev = g.currentEvent;\n    for (let n = 0; ev.phase !== 'play' && n < 400; n++) T.advance(0.05);\n    const key = (code, on) => window.dispatchEvent(new KeyboardEvent(on ? 'keydown' : 'keyup', { code, key: code }));\n    key('KeyC', true); T.advance(0.02); key('KeyC', false); T.advance(0.02);\n    const from = g.input.ringX;\n    key('KeyD', true); T.advance(0.25); key('KeyD', false); T.advance(0.02);\n    const moved = g.input.ringX - from;\n    T.advance(1);\n    const kept = g.input.ringX - from;\n    key('KeyC', true); T.advance(0.02); key('KeyC', false); T.advance(0.02);\n    const back = g.input.ringX;\n    T.goto('menu');\n    return { moved, kept, back };\n  });\n  near('holding a key moves the ring, in .25 s', ring.moved, 0.4, 0.04);\n  ok(Math.abs(ring.kept - ring.moved) < 0.001, 'the ring stays where you leave it', ring.kept.toFixed(3));\n  ok(ring.back === 0, 'C recentres the ring', String(ring.back));\n  await fresh();\n\n  // Plank & Perch: these bots hold the zone better\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 2p notes/issues.md | cut -c1-60; python3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print('interview parses')\"; node tools/build.mjs >/dev/null 2>&1; echo build $?; rm -rf notes/scratch; H=../WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442.html; sha256sum $H | cut -c1-16","description":"Log issues, update hand-ins, add last checks, rebuild"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_0162ghDYSv8BHHJKRFSrHG9A":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-044442__x29b4d9/work/WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442"}}}
