{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F47tjaeVcLfDMx9EtbVcZ5","type":"tool_result","content":"**Title theme motif** (use as written; MIDI, on a 16-step bar, `[step, note, length]`):\n```\nBar 1 D♭maj9: [0,77,3] [3,75,1] [4,73,2] [6,68,4] [12,70,2] [14,72,2]\nBar 2 B♭m9:   [0,73,3] [3,72,1] [4,70,2] [6,65,6] [14,68,2]\nBar 3 E♭m9:   [0,70,3] [3,68,1] [4,66,2] [6,63,4] [12,65,2] [14,66,2]\nBar 4 A♭13:   [0,68,3] [3,70,1] [4,72,2] [6,75,6]\n```\n**Out-of-tune island.** While the rest tilt is above zero, detune every music note by `tilt° × 1.6 × sin(t × 0.7)` cents. At level, it is exactly in tune. The player will feel this before they notice it.\n\n108:    // Starts as bare e-piano of the title theme, then every instrument, slower, in tune.\nsed: -e expression #1, char 1: unknown command: `,'\n26:export function emitBar(track, b, t0, stepDur, fn) {\n27-  const chords = track.chords;\n28-  const chord = parseChord(chords[b % chords.length]);\n29-  const sw = (step) => (step % 2 === 1 ? (track.swing || 0) * stepDur : 0);\n30-  for (const p of track.parts) {\n31-    if (p.from !== undefined && b < p.from) continue;\n32-    if (p.every && b % p.every !== 0) continue;\n33-    if (p.everyBar && b % p.everyBar !== p.everyBar - 1) continue;\n34-    const vel = p.vel ?? 0.5;\n35-    if (p.comp) {\n36-      for (const [s, len] of p.comp) for (const n of chord.notes) fn(t0 + s * stepDur + sw(s), p.inst, n, len * stepDur, vel);\n37-    } else if (p.line) {\n38-      for (const [s, sym, len] of p.line) fn(t0 + s * stepDur + sw(s), p.inst, bassNote(chord, sym) + (p.oct || 0), len * stepD\n39-    } else if (p.hits) {\n40-      for (let s = 0; s < 16; s++) if (p.hits[s] === 'x') fn(t0 + s * stepDur + sw(s), p.inst, p.note || 60, stepDur, vel);\n41-    } else if (p.melody) {\n42-      const bar = p.melody[b % p.melody.length];\n3\n5 notes/scratch/plan.txt","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb93