{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DDvp7HtTVNjZEhrxNLcUde","type":"tool_result","content":"- **Keys in balance events ✔: they move the asking ring, and it stays where you leave it.** Holding a key moves the ring at 1.6 units/s; releasing leaves it there, and C recentres. The ring must be clearly visible on the Balance Disc, because a player steering by keys watches the ring, not the dot. I tested three models with a person-like bot. Keys that spring back on release needed 9.6 presses a second just to hold a pose. A tap-then-accelerate model scored worst (Poses Tier 1: 68 / 75 / 38). This one holds up against the stick: Poses Tier 1 98 / 62 / 54 (stick 100 / 76 / 63), Tier 2 86 / 58 / 34 (90 / 64 / 53), Still Water Tier 1 100 / 85 / 28 (100 / 93 / 24), Fruit Hat Tier 1 21 / 22 / 20 banked with no falls (28 / 33 / 28), Room Service Tier 1 all five glasses. Use a move speed of about 1.6 and don't add acceleration.\n- **Foot keys** ramp 0 to 1 in 0.12 s.\n119:keys poses sharp 100 average 73 clumsy 71 stick 100/98/95\n120:keys stillWater sharp 100 average 24 clumsy 29 stick 100/89/50\n121:keys fruitHat sharp 86 average 56 clumsy 70 stick 91/92/95\n122:keys logReps sharp 97 average 88 clumsy 66 stick 96/81/58\n123:keys roomService sharp 93 average 93 clumsy 93 stick 93/93/93\n124:keys cairn sharp 91 average 91 clumsy 90 stick 92/91/89\n125:mouse poses sharp 100 average 99 clumsy 94 stick 100/98/95\n126:mouse stillWater sharp 100 average 89 clumsy 45 stick 100/89/50\n127:mouse fruitHat sharp 78 average 88 clumsy 96 stick 91/92/95\n128:mouse logReps sharp 97 average 88 clumsy 66 stick 96/81/58\n129:mouse roomService sharp 93 average 93 clumsy 93 stick 93/93/93\n130:mouse cairn sharp 92 average 91 clumsy 89 stick 92/91/89\n131:mouse plates 1.00 0.80\n      if (device === 'keys') {\n        // A person holds a key until the ring is about where they want it.\n        const dx = ax - i.ringX, dz = az - i.ringZ, band = 0.05;\n        key('KeyD', dx > band); key('KeyA', dx < -band); key('KeyS', dz > band); key('KeyW', dz < -band);\n        key('KeyQ', v[6] > 0.5); key('KeyE', v[7] > 0.5); key('KeyF', v[2] > 0.5);\n      } else {\n46:    this.ringX = 0; this.ringZ = 0;\n106:  resetRing() { this.ringX = 0; this.ringZ = 0; this.pointerActive = false; }\n195:      this.ringX += (kx / n) * 1.6 * dt; this.ringZ += (kz / n) * 1.6 * dt;\n196:      const r = Math.hypot(this.ringX, this.ringZ);\n197:      if (r > 1) { this.ringX /= r; this.ringZ /= r; }\n199:    if (pk.has('c')) { this.ringX = 0; this.ringZ = 0; this.pointerActive = false; }\n205:    if (this.pointerActive) { this.ringX = px; this.ringZ = pz; }\n268:      out.wishX = this.ringX; out.wishZ = this.ringZ;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e","uuid":"cd2039b4-0bbb-4a82-a423-0f8623481eed","timestamp":"2026-11-05T19:20:26.121Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- **Keys in balance events ✔: they move the asking ring, and it stays where you leave it.** Holding a key moves the ring at 1.6 units/s; releasing leaves it there, and C recentres. The ring must be clearly visible on the Balance Disc, because a player steering by keys watches the ring, not the dot. I tested three models with a person-like bot. Keys that spring back on release needed 9.6 presses a second just to hold a pose. A tap-then-accelerate model scored worst (Poses Tier 1: 68 / 75 / 38). This one holds up against the stick: Poses Tier 1 98 / 62 / 54 (stick 100 / 76 / 63), Tier 2 86 / 58 / 34 (90 / 64 / 53), Still Water Tier 1 100 / 85 / 28 (100 / 93 / 24), Fruit Hat Tier 1 21 / 22 / 20 banked with no falls (28 / 33 / 28), Room Service Tier 1 all five glasses. Use a move speed of about 1.6 and don't add acceleration.\n- **Foot keys** ramp 0 to 1 in 0.12 s.\n119:keys poses sharp 100 average 73 clumsy 71 stick 100/98/95\n120:keys stillWater sharp 100 average 24 clumsy 29 stick 100/89/50\n121:keys fruitHat sharp 86 average 56 clumsy 70 stick 91/92/95\n122:keys logReps sharp 97 average 88 clumsy 66 stick 96/81/58\n123:keys roomService sharp 93 average 93 clumsy 93 stick 93/93/93\n124:keys cairn sharp 91 average 91 clumsy 90 stick 92/91/89\n125:mouse poses sharp 100 average 99 clumsy 94 stick 100/98/95\n126:mouse stillWater sharp 100 average 89 clumsy 45 stick 100/89/50\n127:mouse fruitHat sharp 78 average 88 clumsy 96 stick 91/92/95\n128:mouse logReps sharp 97 average 88 clumsy 66 stick 96/81/58\n129:mouse roomService sharp 93 average 93 clumsy 93 stick 93/93/93\n130:mouse cairn sharp 92 average 91 clumsy 89 stick 92/91/89\n131:mouse plates 1.00 0.80\n      if (device === 'keys') {\n        // A person holds a key until the ring is about where they want it.\n        const dx = ax - i.ringX, dz = az - i.ringZ, band = 0.05;\n        key('KeyD', dx > band); key('KeyA', dx < -band); key('KeyS', dz > band); key('KeyW', dz < -band);\n        key('KeyQ', v[6] > 0.5); key('KeyE', v[7] > 0.5); key('KeyF', v[2] > 0.5);\n      } else {\n46:    this.ringX = 0; this.ringZ = 0;\n106:  resetRing() { this.ringX = 0; this.ringZ = 0; this.pointerActive = false; }\n195:      this.ringX += (kx / n) * 1.6 * dt; this.ringZ += (kz / n) * 1.6 * dt;\n196:      const r = Math.hypot(this.ringX, this.ringZ);\n197:      if (r > 1) { this.ringX /= r; this.ringZ /= r; }\n199:    if (pk.has('c')) { this.ringX = 0; this.ringZ = 0; this.pointerActive = false; }\n205:    if (this.pointerActive) { this.ringX = px; this.ringZ = pz; }\n268:      out.wishX = this.ringX; out.wishZ = this.ringZ;","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DDvp7HtTVNjZEhrxNLcUde","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
