{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkNbkXHpHGue9D92NtLH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LSWbdti9GqyE5m6KzDZZ7Z","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"O=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-044442__x29b4d9/tmp/claude-1000/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build-v2--20261105-044442--x29b4d9-work/6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e/tasks/bm40ghs3c.output; cut -c1-190 \"$O\"; grep -E \"^on keys\" notes/plan-figures.txt | cut -c1-100; mkdir -p notes/scratch && cat > notes/scratch/last.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\nimport { launch, logicPage, root } from '../../tools/lib.mjs';\nconst iv = JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(root, 'exit-interview.json'), 'utf8'));\nconst b = await launch(); const p = await logicPage(b);\nconst about = await p.evaluate(() => { const T = window.__TEST__; T.goto('about'); T.advance(0.05); const top = T.game.ui.top; let s = ''; const n = top.pages; for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { s += ` ${document.querySelector('.about').textContent}`; top.turn(1); T.advance(0.01); } T.goto('menu'); return { n, s: s.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ') }; });\nconst vals = [...Object.values(iv.sourceInformation), ...iv.testingFeedback, ...iv.engineFeedback, ...iv.promptFeedback];\nconst sent = vals.flatMap((v) => v.split(/(?<=[.!?])\\s+/)).map((x) => x.trim()).filter(Boolean);\nconst miss = sent.filter((x) => !about.s.includes(x));\nconsole.log(`About: ${about.n} pages, ${vals.length} values, ${sent.length} sentences, ${miss.length} missing`); miss.forEach((m) => console.log('MISSING', m.slice(0, 110)));\nawait b.close();\nEOF\nfor i in $(seq 1 60); do a=$(awk '/MemAvailable/{print int($2/1048576)}' /proc/meminfo); [ \"$a\" -ge 2 ] && break; sleep 10; done; timeout 90 node notes/scratch/last.mjs 2>&1 | cut -c1-150; rm -rf notes/scratch; ls notes | tr '\\n' ' '; echo; sha256sum ../WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442.html | cut -c1-16; grep -rnE \"\\b(TODO|FIXME)\\b|placeholder|\\bstub\\b\" src | wc -l; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\niv=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'))\nprint(iv['sourceInformation']['testing'])\nfor i,a in enumerate(iv['testingFeedback']): print(i+1,a[:70],'...')\nprint(iv['engineFeedback'][1])\nEOF","description":"Read the final run, compare About, print the hand-in text","timeout":400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":480,"cache_read_input_tokens":650883,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":480},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e","uuid":"1bd8f66a-9a01-4238-8232-bbe698549d46","timestamp":"2026-11-05T19:58:52.236Z","request_id":"req_011CgkNbk1XK7JELb8bpC1Nh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LSWbdti9GqyE5m6KzDZZ7Z":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-044442__x29b4d9/work/WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442 && O=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-044442__x29b4d9/tmp/claude-1000/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build-v2--20261105-044442--x29b4d9-work/6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e/tasks/bm40ghs3c.output; cut -c1-190 \"$O\"; grep -E \"^on keys\" notes/plan-figures.txt | cut -c1-100; mkdir -p notes/scratch && cat > notes/scratch/last.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\nimport { launch, logicPage, root } from '../../tools/lib.mjs';\nconst iv = JSON.parse(readFileSync(join(root, 'exit-interview.json'), 'utf8'));\nconst b = await launch(); const p = await logicPage(b);\nconst about = await p.evaluate(() => { const T = window.__TEST__; T.goto('about'); T.advance(0.05); const top = T.game.ui.top; let s = ''; const n = top.pages; for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { s += ` ${document.querySelector('.about').textContent}`; top.turn(1); T.advance(0.01); } T.goto('menu'); return { n, s: s.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ') }; });\nconst vals = [...Object.values(iv.sourceInformation), ...iv.testingFeedback, ...iv.engineFeedback, ...iv.promptFeedback];\nconst sent = vals.flatMap((v) => v.split(/(?<=[.!?])\\s+/)).map((x) => x.trim()).filter(Boolean);\nconst miss = sent.filter((x) => !about.s.includes(x));\nconsole.log(`About: ${about.n} pages, ${vals.length} values, ${sent.length} sentences, ${miss.length} missing`); miss.forEach((m) => console.log('MISSING', m.slice(0, 110)));\nawait b.close();\nEOF\nfor i in $(seq 1 60); do a=$(awk '/MemAvailable/{print int($2/1048576)}' /proc/meminfo); [ \"$a\" -ge 2 ] && break; sleep 10; done; timeout 90 node notes/scratch/last.mjs 2>&1 | cut -c1-150; rm -rf notes/scratch; ls notes | tr '\\n' ' '; echo; sha256sum ../WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442.html | cut -c1-16; grep -rnE \"\\b(TODO|FIXME)\\b|placeholder|\\bstub\\b\" src | wc -l; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\niv=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'))\nprint(iv['sourceInformation']['testing'])\nfor i,a in enumerate(iv['testingFeedback']): print(i+1,a[:70],'...')\nprint(iv['engineFeedback'][1])\nEOF","description":"Read the final run, compare About, print the hand-in text","timeout":400000}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01LSWbdti9GqyE5m6KzDZZ7Z":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-044442__x29b4d9/work/WeFib-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-044442"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LSWbdti9GqyE5m6KzDZZ7Z","type":"tool_result","content":"17:    this.skillName = skill; this.s = SKILLS[skill] || SKILLS.average;\nfree GB at start: 3\nbefore 999f0b4e74024aeb\nexit 0\nafter  999f0b4e74024aeb\nunit     1272 passed, 0 failed\nflow     93 passed, 0 failed\nevents   296 passed, 0 failed\nbalance  152 passed, 0 failed\nplan     351 passed, 0 failed\ninput    44 passed, 0 failed\naudio    175 passed, 0 failed\nhub      9 passed, 0 failed\nui       68 passed, 0 failed\n2460 passed, 0 failed\n\n[exited with code 0]\non keys Poses T1 95 / 80 / 67 plan 98 / 62 / 54\non keys Poses T2 79 / 61 / 49 plan 86 / 58 / 34\non keys Still Water T1 in the zone 100 / 92 / 71 plan 100 / 85 / 28\non keys Fruit Hat T1 banked 23 / 24 / 28 plan 21 / 22 / 20\non keys Room Service T1 glasses 5 / 5 / 5 plan 5 / 5 / 5\nAbout: 15 pages, 29 values, 48 sentences, 0 missing\nhub-README.md issues.md plan-figures.txt \n999f0b4e74024aeb\n0\nAllowed: as much headless testing as wanted, scripts that play the game and check its state including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, one command printing only failures and a one-line count, screenshots only for what a script can't check, no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Ran: node tools/test.mjs with nine groups and about 2,440 checks: whole-game playthrough by bots on a stubbed pad, every event and tier, balance tables over three seeds, the figures PLAN.md measured played against the build, gameplay, art recipes and audio, the same bots again through real key and pointer events, every verb on pad, keys and mouse, offline audio renders, the hub harness at 1, 2 and 4 players, bad network and host leaving, the 1080p layout audit, touch profiles, a WebGL2 boot in WebKit, plus a screenshot art pass. Not run: real controller, real TV, human ears, a human player.\n1 76 logged in notes/issues.md as they happened: 64 caught by test scrip ...\n2 14: Hop presses lost during hit-stop, every Tug of Peace doll falling, ...\n3 The scripted whole-game playthrough with bots on a stubbed pad. It got ...\n4 The Dev Mode slider test as I first wrote it. It compared a number wit ...\nYes. Rapier panics caught me most: disabling a core after removing its joint panicked world.step on a later dive, and every call after that reported a misleading recursive-use error. I first took that for a bug in my own test. I also guessed wrong on instance colours: a mesh first drawn before any setColorAt stays white for good. And my own collision filter let the island walker fall through the ground for most of the build: nothing read its height, so nothing showed it.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6048a4b4-78b7-4200-a8b0-b745f5bb937e","uuid":"dbe8f093-8b04-4267-8fdd-d89e8b69a7fc","timestamp":"2026-11-05T19:58:53.598Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"17:    this.skillName = skill; this.s = SKILLS[skill] || SKILLS.average;\nfree GB at start: 3\nbefore 999f0b4e74024aeb\nexit 0\nafter  999f0b4e74024aeb\nunit     1272 passed, 0 failed\nflow     93 passed, 0 failed\nevents   296 passed, 0 failed\nbalance  152 passed, 0 failed\nplan     351 passed, 0 failed\ninput    44 passed, 0 failed\naudio    175 passed, 0 failed\nhub      9 passed, 0 failed\nui       68 passed, 0 failed\n2460 passed, 0 failed\n\n[exited with code 0]\non keys Poses T1 95 / 80 / 67 plan 98 / 62 / 54\non keys Poses T2 79 / 61 / 49 plan 86 / 58 / 34\non keys Still Water T1 in the zone 100 / 92 / 71 plan 100 / 85 / 28\non keys Fruit Hat T1 banked 23 / 24 / 28 plan 21 / 22 / 20\non keys Room Service T1 glasses 5 / 5 / 5 plan 5 / 5 / 5\nAbout: 15 pages, 29 values, 48 sentences, 0 missing\nhub-README.md issues.md plan-figures.txt \n999f0b4e74024aeb\n0\nAllowed: as much headless testing as wanted, scripts that play the game and check its state including a scripted playthrough of the whole game, one command printing only failures and a one-line count, screenshots only for what a script can't check, no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. Ran: node tools/test.mjs with nine groups and about 2,440 checks: whole-game playthrough by bots on a stubbed pad, every event and tier, balance tables over three seeds, the figures PLAN.md measured played against the build, gameplay, art recipes and audio, the same bots again through real key and pointer events, every verb on pad, keys and mouse, offline audio renders, the hub harness at 1, 2 and 4 players, bad network and host leaving, the 1080p layout audit, touch profiles, a WebGL2 boot in WebKit, plus a screenshot art pass. Not run: real controller, real TV, human ears, a human player.\n1 76 logged in notes/issues.md as they happened: 64 caught by test scrip ...\n2 14: Hop presses lost during hit-stop, every Tug of Peace doll falling, ...\n3 The scripted whole-game playthrough with bots on a stubbed pad. It got ...\n4 The Dev Mode slider test as I first wrote it. It compared a number wit ...\nYes. Rapier panics caught me most: disabling a core after removing its joint panicked world.step on a later dive, and every call after that reported a misleading recursive-use error. I first took that for a bug in my own test. I also guessed wrong on instance colours: a mesh first drawn before any setColorAt stays white for good. And my own collision filter let the island walker fall through the ground for most of the build: nothing read its height, so nothing showed it.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LSWbdti9GqyE5m6KzDZZ7Z","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
